# Test: ze completion words -- non-env commands must not contain env children
# VALIDATES: wireEnvHints does not pollute arbitrary command trees
# PREVENTS: env appearing as a subcommand of bgp, signal, config, etc.
#
# Each reject= reads only the output of the cmd= line above it
# (Record.assertionTarget, record_parse.go), so every command carries its own.
#
# A completion record is name-TAB-summary (completion-words-summary.ci), so the
# anchored pattern says what this test forbids -- a candidate NAMED env -- and
# does not rot when a summary changes. The bare substring `env` this file used
# to carry was clean only while no summary in these three trees said
# "environment".

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze completion words bgp:exit=0
reject=stdout:pattern=(?m)^env\t

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze completion words signal:exit=0
reject=stdout:pattern=(?m)^env\t

cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze completion words config:exit=0
expect=exit:code=0
reject=stdout:pattern=(?m)^env\t
